'''Reverse Quad Draft''' is a 2on2 non-eliminating tournament meant for rookies and low/mid-skilled players. One can think of it as the 2on2 Edition of [[QuakeWorld MIX League]].

Signups are to be approved by the admin - we want to limit the tournament to lower-skilled players, coming mostly from the QML ranks. '''Signups will be taken in batches of 4''', to keep the number of teams even (thus no byes need to be used).

Players will be seeded based on the earlier results of the players, at the discretion of an admin. The players are split into upper- and lower-half pools. A draft will be held on '''Sunday 26th of April, 19:00-19:30 CET''', in the QML discord ([https://discord.com/channels/1306206890115469443/1494267775932436531 #rqd-players-only]), where the '''lower-half pool''' players pick their playing partners from the '''upper-half pool''' of players. First pick is the lowest seed, second pick is the second lowest seed, etc. until all picks are done. If you wish to be paired with a specific player, you can state so at the beginning of the draft so the pickers can take that into account. '''If you cannot come to the draft to pick your partner, an admin will pair you with the highest available seed.'''   This draft is only done at the beginning of the tournament, i.e. the whole tournament will be played with the same teams - no new draft for every round.

Stand-ins at +2 to -2 of seed position from within RQD can be used without approval. If such a stand-in is not available, other stand-ins can be used if the opposing team approves of the stand-in.

A non-eliminating tournament structure ('''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swiss-system_tournament Swiss]''') will be used. Number of rounds played is dependent on signups, with a maximum of 4 rounds.

All matches are Best of 5 (BO5).

== Format ==
* '''Swiss'''
* All matches are BO5.
* Up to 4 rounds of matches, 1 match per week.
* No divisions, no regions.
* First round of pairings will be posted on April 26th.

